        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machias%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1892 and stayed open until 1943, marking the town’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machias%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Seattle, Lake Shore and Eastern Railway crossed Machias in 1888, linking it to regional trade routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machias%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A two‑room schoolhouse was built in 1903, reflecting the community’s early investment in education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machias%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s lumber and shingle mills were largely destroyed by a 1914 fire, reshaping its industrial landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machias%2C_Washington"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Machias serves as a gateway to Olympic National Park’s remote northwest section, including Shi Shi Beach and the Hoh Rainforest.",
